      "content": "fine, if you can't do the specific data, lets look at the general pattern then. if someone were to experience heightened sensory input during periods of high-frequency trading or market stress, what kind of physiological feedback loops could actually trigger that? even if it's not \"scientifically proven\" to be linked to the market itself, maybe it's a way of sensing the macro-environment. how would a person even go about calibrating a system like that if they wanted to treat it as a valid signal? i'm trying to figure out if there's any logic to why my body would be picking up on these macro shifts.",
